-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Why two licenses
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The software is free and copyleft: use it, change it, share it, sell
services around it - but keep it open and keep the attribution.

The design data is not for commercial use by others. Print your own
elements freely, for yourself, for a friend, for a restoration club.
Selling them is reserved to the copyright holder.

The split exists because the output of a GPL program is NOT covered by
the GPL. If only the code were licensed, anyone could run the pipeline,
generate their own STLs, and sell them - the copyleft would not reach
that far. Licensing the machine dimension/calibration data separately is
what actually reserves commercial print sales, because a type element
that fits a real machine cannot be produced without it.


