-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Prior art
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

RobertG's OpenSCAD Blickensderfer type wheel generator
(badonoer.blogspot.com, CC BY-SA 4.0, March 2025) was read and compared
against v4 in detail - see SESSION_LOG.md part 85. Several config
comments credit it by name.

What was taken from it is ideas and problem statements, not expression:
that a font's caret sits at cap height rather than on the baseline and
needs a per-character Y offset, that the underscore has the mirrored
problem, and that a wheel can carry notched or banded cosmetics. Each
was then implemented independently in v4's own code and its own config
sections. No source text was copied.

The dimensional values did not come from him either. v4's were ported
from v2, which predates his generator; part 85 records the two sets
converging to within 0.025mm from unrelated derivations, and uses that
as a cross-check, not a source. Physical measurements of a hundred-year-
old machine are facts in any case, which copyright does not reach.

This matters because his work is ShareAlike and this project's design
data is NonCommercial, which ShareAlike would not permit in a derivative
work. Ideas, methods and measured facts are not protected by copyright,
so no derivative work exists and the ShareAlike term is not triggered.
The credit in the configs is given because it is deserved, not because a
license compels it. If anything is ever ported from that project as
actual code or copied text, this reasoning stops applying and the
affected files would need to be CC BY-SA 4.0 (compatible with the GPL
one-way, but not with a NonCommercial term).


